#   data item format specifiers for SECS-II messages. These are private variables
#   uncomment these only if you need something other than U4 format.  Format conversion degrades performance.
#4040=ALIDFormat,the data type for alarm ids in messages,,SV,U4,,1,0,U4 1,U4 11,U4 7,ALIDFormat
#4041=CEIDFormat,the data type for CE ids in messages,,SV,U4,,1,0,U4 1,U4 11,U4 7,CEIDFormat
#4042=DATAIDFormat,the data type for DATAID in messages,,SV,U4,,1,0,U4 1,U4 11,U4 7,DATAIDFormat
#4043=RPTIDFormat,the data type for report ids in messages,,SV,U4,,1,0,U4 1,U4 11,U4 7,RPTIDFormat
#4044=TRIDFormat,the data type for trace ids in messages,,SV,U4,,1,0,U4 1,U4 11,U4 7,TRIDFormat
#4045=VIDFormat,the data type for variable (EC SV DV) ids in messages,,SV,U4,,1,0,U4 1,U4 11,U4 7,VIDFormat
#   data item format specifiers for incoming SECS-II messages. These are private variables
#   are used to validate data items in incoming messages from GEM host.  If a variable is
#   missing (commented out), set to an empty L list value or has invalid format
#   the value of coresponding XXXFormat variable is used (see above).
4050=ALIDInputFormat,allowed data type for alarm ids (ALID) in messages from host,,SV,U4,,1,0,,,U4 7 8 6 5,ALIDInputFormat
4051=CEIDInputFormat,allowed data type for collection event ids (CEID) in messages from host,,SV,U4,,1,0,,,U4 7 8 6 5,CEIDInputFormat
4052=DATAIDInputFormat,allowed data type for data ids (DATAID) in messages from host,,SV,U4,,1,0,,,U4 7 8 6 5,DATAIDInputFormat
4053=RPTIDInputFormat,allowed data type for report ids (RPTID) in messages from host,,SV,U4,,1,0,,,U4 7 8 6 5,RPTIDInputFormat
4054=TRIDInputFormat,allowed data type for trace ids (TRID) in messages from host,,SV,U4,,1,0,,,U4 7 8 6 5,TRIDInputFormat
4055=VIDInputFormat,allowed data type for variable (EC SV DV) ids in messages from host,,SV,U4,,1,0,,,U4 7 8 6 5,VIDInputFormat

301000=MaxSimultaneousTraces,The maximum number of traces that can be requested simultaneously from the host,,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 10,MaxSimultaneousTraces
301001=MaxTraceFrequency,The maximum rate at which a host can request a trace report to be delivered,ms,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 100,MaxTraceFrequency
301002=MaxTraceVIDs,The maximum number of VIDs that can be requested for any single trace report,,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 500,MaxTraceVIDs
301003=S1F3WaitForGetValue,This value represents a threshold for how long to wait on any data registered for a GetValue callback.  If the number is 0 it will wait indefinitely.,ms,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 40,S1F3WaitForGetValue
301004=TraceDataWaitForGetValue,This value represents a threshold for how long to wait on any data registered for a GetValue callback.  If the number is 0 it will wait indefinitely.  If the number is greater than the currently requested trace interval it will be adjusted internally to equal the trace interval,ms,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 100,TraceDataWaitForGetValue
301005=VariableReportingStyle,0 = Strict compliance with SEMI standards; 1 = Allow any variable type (SV; DV; or EC) to be reported both for S1F3 and Trace reports,,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 1,VariableReportingStyle
301006=TraceTimestampTolerance,The allowable variation for any given trace report's timestamp from the expected timestamp,ms,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 20,TraceTimestampTolerance
301007=ReportGenerationDelay,This value represents the expected amount of time it takes CIMConnect to build a 500 VID Report.  This number will be subtracted from the allowed wait time for either an S1F3 request or a Trace Report.,ms,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 20,ReportGenerationDelay
301008=TraceReportMultiBlock,This variable represents whether or not CIMConnect can automatically send a multi-block message for Trace Reports that are larger than 244 bytes (0 = do not send multi-bock trace reports. 1[default] = send multi-block trace reports),,EC,U4,,0,1,,,U4 1,TraceReportMultiBlock
301009=ReportOfflineControlState,When transitioning to Offline control state report CONTROLSTATE as Offline (1=enable 0=default),,EC,Bo,,1,0,Bo 0,Bo 1,Bo 1,ReportOfflineControlState
